One common way the Java API can be misused is through improper handling of user input when interacting with the system shell. This can lead to Command Injection vulnerabilities.

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;

public class CommandExecutor {
    public void pingHost(String hostname) throws Exception {
        // The following line is vulnerable to command injection because 
        // it uses a single string containing user input in Runtime.getRuntime().exec().
        // An attacker could provide input like "google.com; rm -rf /"
        String command = "ping -c 1 " + hostname;
        Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            System.out.println(line);
        }
    }
}
```

